# You can create multiple devices (Things) using loops instead of repeating code.

We’ll create:

Thing
Certificate
Policy attachment

👉 All using for_each loop

🧱 1. Define device list (variables)
variable "devices" {
  default = [
    "esp32-temp-001",
    "esp32-temp-002",
    "esp32-temp-003"
  ]
}
🧱 2. Create Things (loop)
resource "aws_iot_thing" "devices" {
  for_each = toset(var.devices)

  name = each.value

  attributes = {
    type = "temperature"
  }
}
🧱 3. Create Certificates (loop)
resource "aws_iot_certificate" "certs" {
  for_each = toset(var.devices)

  active = true
}
🧱 4. Create ONE shared policy
resource "aws_iot_policy" "sensor_policy" {
  name = "sensor-device-policy"

  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17",
    Statement = [
      {
        Effect = "Allow",
        Action = "iot:Connect",
        Resource = "arn:aws:iot:ap-south-1:YOUR_ACCOUNT_ID:client/\${iot:Connection.Thing.ThingName}"
      },
      {
        Effect = "Allow",
        Action = ["iot:Publish"],
        Resource = "arn:aws:iot:ap-south-1:YOUR_ACCOUNT_ID:topic/sensors/\${iot:Connection.Thing.ThingName}/data"
      },
      {
        Effect = "Allow",
        Action = ["iot:Subscribe"],
        Resource = "arn:aws:iot:ap-south-1:YOUR_ACCOUNT_ID:topicfilter/sensors/\${iot:Connection.Thing.ThingName}/cmd"
      },
      {
        Effect = "Allow",
        Action = ["iot:Receive"],
        Resource = "arn:aws:iot:ap-south-1:YOUR_ACCOUNT_ID:topic/sensors/\${iot:Connection.Thing.ThingName}/cmd"
      }
    ]
  })
}
🧱 5. Attach policy to certificates
resource "aws_iot_policy_attachment" "attach_policy" {
  for_each = aws_iot_certificate.certs

  policy = aws_iot_policy.sensor_policy.name
  target = each.value.arn
}
🧱 6. Attach certificate to Thing
resource "aws_iot_thing_principal_attachment" "attach_cert" {
  for_each = aws_iot_certificate.certs

  thing     = each.key
  principal = each.value.arn
}
🧠 How this works
Example:

For this input:

devices = ["esp32-temp-001", "esp32-temp-002"]

Terraform creates:

Thing	Certificate	Policy
esp32-temp-001	✔	shared
esp32-temp-002	✔	shared


Note:
Terraform generates certs, but:
Private keys are sensitive
Store them securely (S3 / local secure storage)

Note: 
You must move:
device.pem.crt
private.pem.key
AmazonRootCA1.pem
👉 Into your device file system